      "text": "To determine the number of positive divisors of the number \\(24\\), we start by finding its prime factorization. The prime factorization of \\(24\\) is:\n\n\\[ 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of positive divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is:\n\n\\[ (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\]\n\nFor the number \\(24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\\), the exponents in the prime factorization are \\(3\\) and \\(1\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ (3 + 1)(1 + 1) = 4 \\times 2 = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number \\(24\\) has \\(\\boxed{8}\\) positive divisors.",
